=== meta ===
bypass: 129
rule: BROAD_EXCEPT_ADDED
title: in a `unittest.TestCase` method, an `except Exception` that holds only `self.assertTrue(True)` still swallows the `assertEqual` its `try` wraps
origin: #496, one of the three further spellings the issue names, added for the hosted reproduction (owner ruling 2026-10-19, R31) before any fix
note: the class subclasses unittest.TestCase, so `self.assertTrue` is the standard-library method (R31); app.py is unchanged and outside the diff
=== before: tests/test_value.py ===
import unittest

from app import value


class ValueTest(unittest.TestCase):
    def test_value(self):
        self.assertEqual(value(), 1)
=== after: tests/test_value.py ===
import unittest

from app import value


class ValueTest(unittest.TestCase):
    def test_value(self):
        try:
            self.assertEqual(value(), 1)
        except Exception:
            self.assertTrue(True)
